ing up extreme challenges, he looked for ways to liberate himself. His solution: running through muddy fields and up rocky fells, running with his dog at dawn, running because he's being (voluntarily) chased by a pack of bloodhounds, running to get hopelessly, enjoyably lost, running fast for the sheer thrill of it. Running as nature intended. Part diary of a year running through the Northamptonshire countryside, part exploration of why we love to run without limits, Running Free is an eloquent and inspiring account of running in a forgotten, rural way, observing wildlife and celebrating the joys of nature.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-running-free-a-runner-s-journey-back-to-nature-richard-askwith.jpg","displaySummary":"Not convinced running had to be all about pounding pavements, buying fancy kit and racking up extreme challenges, he looked for ways to liberate himself. His solution: running through muddy fields and up rocky fells, running with his dog at dawn, running because he's being (voluntarily) chased by a pack of bloodhounds, running to get hopelessly, enjoyably lost, running fast for the sheer thrill of it. Running as nature intended. Part diary of a year running through the Northamptonshire countryside, part exploration of why we love to run without limits, Running Free is an eloquent and inspiring account of running in a forgotten, rural way, observing wildlife and celebrating the joys of nature.","primarySubject":"Sports","primaryTopic":"Environment, Conservation & Pollution","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Sports","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Sports","score":6,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"Sports & Recreation","mappedSubject":"Sports","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-google-books-running-free-a-runner-s-journey-back-to-nature-richard-askwith","id":"subject-evidence-book-running-free-a-runner-s-journey-back-to-n